SUMMARY:Second Nature: Documentary Screening with Dame Judi Dentures & Frie
 nds
LOCATION:CitySpace\, 43 Main St\, Easthampton\, MA 01027
DESCRIPTION:Film Screening + Drag Performances + Reception with Local Queer
  and Trans Organizations\nSecond Nature: Documenting Queer Gender and Sexu
 ality in the Animal World A Documentary Produced and Narrated by Elliot Pa
 ge Sunday\, November 29 4-6:30pm The Rooted Co-op and Dame Judi Dentures P
 roductions present a free community screening of Second Nature\, Elliot Pa
 ge’s funny\, heartwarming documentary about queer and trans diversity in
  the animal world. The afternoon will begin with drag performances by Dame
  Judi Dentures and other local artists\, followed by the film screening\, 
 and then a reception with resource tables from local LGBTQ+-affirming orga
 nizations including TransHealth and Translate Gender. Sliding scale ticket
 s (with a free option!) support event costs and free screenings of the fil
 m for LGBTQIA+ youth in states where inclusive sex ed is banned. All are w
 elcome. We highly recommend reserving a spot in advance\, as capacity is l
 imited. Reserve your spot here.\nhttps://givebutter.com/second_nature_scre
 ening_nov_29\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://givebutter.com/second_nature_screening_nov_29
END:VEVENT
